  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we visit a reed bed. A nature reserve with reeds, a few pools and a hide is one of the best places to practise bird watching, and all five of today's birds live there, or on a river nearby.\n\nReed bed birds are easy to hear and hard to see. In spring they sing from the top of a stem, which gives you a few seconds to look. On the open water, grebes are much easier: they dive, but they come up again. And then there is the one everyone wants to see, a flash of electric blue along the river.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
